==== hyperbricks yaml {!{page}} ====
page:
  - type: hypermedia
  - route: duplicate-item-names-deep

  - content:
      - type: tree

      - section_block:
          - type: tree

          - article_block:
              - type: tree

              - copy:
                  - type: text
                  - value: First copy

              - copy:
                  - type: text
                  - value: Second copy
==== explainer ====
Duplicate child-name recovery is local to the nested TREE where the duplicate occurs.
Deep nested composite maps still emit accurate local @order data.
==== expected json ====
{
  "@order": [
    "content"
  ],
  "@type": "<HYPERMEDIA>",
  "content": {
    "@order": [
      "section_block"
    ],
    "@type": "<TREE>",
    "section_block": {
      "@order": [
        "article_block"
      ],
      "@type": "<TREE>",
      "article_block": {
        "@order": [
          "copy",
          "copy_2"
        ],
        "@type": "<TREE>",
        "copy": {
          "@type": "<TEXT>",
          "value": "First copy"
        },
        "copy_2": {
          "@type": "<TEXT>",
          "value": "Second copy"
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "route": "duplicate-item-names-deep"
}
==== expected diagnostics ====
[
  {
    "type": "YAML",
    "path": "page.content.section_block.article_block",
    "key": "copy",
    "level": "WARNING",
    "contains": "using \"copy_2\" as runtime path"
  }
]
==== expected output ====
<!DOCTYPE html><html><body>First copySecond copy</body></html>
